{"name":"Mariana Trench","hex":"#445956","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mariana Trench","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A submarine trench in the North Pacific Ocean, noted for having the deepest known point on Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mariana_Trench"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mariana Trench","blocks":[{"text":"The Mariana Trench is the deepest oceanic trench on Earth, located in the western Pacific Ocean, about 200 kilometers (124 mi) east of the Mariana Islands. It is crescent-shaped and measures about 2,550 km (1,580 mi) in length and 69 km (43 mi) in width. The maximum known depth is 10,935 ± 6 meters at the southern end of a small slot-shaped valley in its floor known as the Challenger Deep. This makes the deepest point of the trench more than 2 km (1.2 mi) farther from sea level than the peak of Mount Everest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Marianatrenchmap.png/330px-Marianatrenchmap.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariana_Trench","wikidata":"Q510"},{"title":"Trench","blocks":[{"text":"A trench is a type of excavation or depression in the ground that is generally deeper than it is wide, and narrow compared with its length."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Polyethylene_gas_main.jpg/330px-Polyethylene_gas_main.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trench","wikidata":"Q1852785"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Bathyscaphe_Trieste.jpg/500px-Bathyscaphe_Trieste.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Bathyscaphe_Trieste.jpg/1280px-Bathyscaphe_Trieste.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src